 are  going to be so important because we may  finally get an answer to this  darksaber's true nature like why is its  hum more of a song why is its blade flat  and it's edged cracked why is its color  black i mean according to kane and  jairus there is a kyber crystal in that  hilt but what of experience did tar  vizsla have on ilum to unearth an ebony  colored crystal it can't just be that  tar was a goth i mean with a name like  tar really i see two futures for the  dark saber one it could end up in the  hands of grogu a bit of george lucasian  poetry for this latest foundling to have  a shared custody between the jedi and  the mandalorians to inherit the artifact  of the mandalorian jedi tarvisla since  neither the dark saber nor grogu appear  in the sequel films that could explain  their shared absence but based on the  design the color the unusual nature of  this lightsaber it feels like a  violation of nature i think a more  fitting destiny for the dark saber is  for it and it's black olson kyber  crystal to be destroyed permanently its  edge is cracked as if it wants to be  destroyed as if it is trying to tear  itself apart it has made itself a pain  in the ass for everyone who has carried  it really it's less of an excalibur than  a ring of sauron it has never truly  united any mandalorians we have followed  on any of these titles really it has  just kept them at war with each other  and i think the recent episode of the  mandalorian hinted at this by pointing  out that the darksaber's hilt is made of  besguard the hilt is of a quality of  bhaskar i have never seen before which  the armorer said in reference to the  spear mandalorian steel is meant for  armor not weapons therefore the dark  saber's existence is a violation to  their own creed so ultimately it was not  that bo-katan wielded a darksaber  unjustly when she tried to unite the  mandalorians at the end of rebels it was  that she had to hold a sword at all to  do that so preach living waters of  m